# The restore drill's timer (SPEC-064 R5, R6; ADR-064): Sundays at 06:24, a minute of the hour that
# no job of the table, no reserved slot and no minute of the predecessor's schedule holds. A run
# missed while the host was down is made up at the next start, and a short random delay keeps it out
# of step with the other timers. The calendar is written in UTC; the private rail renders it in the
# owner's zone. With no Unit=, the timer starts the service of its own name.
[Unit]
Description=DeckStreak's restore drill, once a week

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Sun *-*-* 06:24:00 UTC
Persistent=true
RandomizedDelaySec=30s
AccuracySec=1us

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
